menuconfig ZMK_LIVE_FEED
    bool "Live key/layer feed over BLE NOTIFY (Torabo-Float)"
    depends on BT && (!ZMK_SPLIT || ZMK_SPLIT_ROLE_CENTRAL)
    default n
    help
      Push a small packed event on every key press/release and layer change over a
      dedicated NOTIFY GATT service (e1f4af00), so a desktop overlay (Torabo-Float)
      can show which key is being pressed and which layer is active in real time.

      CENTRAL-only: only the central knows the layer state and the global key
      position. The push is fire-and-forget and only fires while a client has
      subscribed the CCC, so an unused build pays nothing. See Torabo-Float/PLAN.md.

      Default n; enable per build target with the torabo-live-feed snippet.

if ZMK_LIVE_FEED

config ZMK_LIVE_FEED_TUNNEL
    bool "Expose the live feed over the Studio RPC torabo tunnel"
    depends on ZMK_STUDIO_TORABO_TUNNEL
    default y
    help
      Also push the feed through the torabo tunnel (feature id 0x0F), so a Float
      connected over USB receives the same 16-byte records as a BLE subscriber.
      Key/layer and diagnostic records share one stream here; evt_type already
      tells them apart. Pushes only happen while a client has sent SUBSCRIBE, and
      that subscription is dropped when the client becomes unreachable, so an
      unused build still pays nothing.

config ZMK_LIVE_FEED_PREF_LATENCY
    int "Preferred peripheral latency while a client is subscribed"
    default 10
    help
      Connection latency requested when a client subscribes the feed. The default
      peripheral latency batches notifications into a laggy burst; a lower value is
      requested on subscribe and restored on unsubscribe (mirrors the Studio RPC
      transport). Only requested when this is below CONFIG_BT_PERIPHERAL_PREF_LATENCY.

config ZMK_LIVE_FEED_THREAD_STACK_SIZE
    int "Live feed notify thread stack size"
    default 1536 if ZMK_LIVE_FEED_TUNNEL
    default 1024
    help
      Stack for the dedicated live_feed work queue thread. This thread owns the
      bt_gatt_notify() call, which blocks (K_FOREVER) when the ACL TX buffers are
      exhausted, and also runs compute_keymap_crc(). Sized like ZMK's own BLE
      notify thread (CONFIG_ZMK_BLE_THREAD_STACK_SIZE, the HOG send queue) with a
      little extra headroom for the CRC walk.

      With the tunnel on, the same thread also encodes a protobuf Notification
      and runs nanopb's encoder, hence the higher default.

config ZMK_LIVE_FEED_THREAD_PRIORITY
    int "Live feed notify thread priority"
    default 10
    help
      Priority of the dedicated live_feed work queue thread. A preemptible, low
      priority (matching ZMK's low-priority work queue used by RGB/battery) keeps
      this best-effort overlay feature from ever preempting key scanning, HID, or
      split traffic; when its bt_gatt_notify() blocks it only pends itself.

config ZMK_LIVE_FEED_DIAG_HEARTBEAT_MS
    int "Diagnostic heartbeat interval (ms)"
    default 750
    help
      Diagnostic mode (per-device liveness on the second characteristic e1f4af02,
      PLAN-torabo-float.md §13) ships with the live feed. On-change records are cheap
      and always sent; a periodic heartbeat runs only while a client opts in (writes
      1 to e1f4af02), re-sending every device's record this often so the app can show
      "N ms ago" freshness and pick up the encoder counters (which have no input-event
      hook). Only runs while a client has it enabled, so a normal user pays nothing.

module = ZMK_LIVE_FEED
module-str = ZMK Live Feed
source "subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_config"

endif # ZMK_LIVE_FEED
